{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:45b1346368fc72f4","name":"Ion Mine","source":{"id":"source:reference-45b1346368fc72f4","title":"Ion Mine","revision":20884,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:42:50Z","sha256":"dba2ed7ea413fb7784be06049a85b0a831f222ce043648edec969f16cdd57b59","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20884","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Ion%20Mine&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-45b1346368fc72f4","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 800\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 0.5 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Availability:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Ion Mines can disable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," without causing lasting harm, allowing them to be captured or salvaged later on. An Ion Mine is placed in or on the ground (in any square adjacent to you) and is triggered when any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ground Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ground_Vehicle"}," enters the Mine's square. An Ion Mine deals ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion"}," damage to everything in a 2-Square ",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"}," radius.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Mines are designed for placement in the ground or to be otherwise hidden from sight. Any character attempting to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Notice"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Notice"}," a Mine takes a -5 penalty to his or her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," check. Setting a Mine is a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," and does not require a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check. However, attaching a detonator (either Timed or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Manual_Trigger","referenceId":"reference:3bac33a88449a688"},") requires a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check and overrides the Mine's built-in triggering system.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Size:"]}," Tiny\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 8d6 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Ion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ion"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Radius:"]}," 2-Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Burst"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Burst"},")\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
